:answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3e187ae-ec73-5aa1-9abb-af1c37a04e5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117964} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f43defc-60eb-5fef-a664-a3e6a18cbfdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117963}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cc1044df-5089-5bf6-ad79-aebf9c199eb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-34207" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c},$ $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨1,5,8⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨-1,-1,-3⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨-3,5,-7⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s-t=-3 \\\\ 5s-t=5 \\\\ 8s-3t=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -7\\end{array}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -7\\end{array}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 17\\end{array}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 17\\end{array}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{array}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-8,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3734c4e7-2d56-58b9-ae64-9d84eccc2689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315439} {:answer/id #uuid "8db74fb0-e83b-5025-b902-46b7c22dbba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315912} {:answer/id #uuid "aac648fc-10fc-5899-80de-3f61d32db10b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316080} {:answer/id #uuid "bf12471c-beac-5673-aa1a-61bae4ae90c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316195} {:answer/id #uuid "ebbf0643-15ef-58aa-bbc9-12b0a9c98f7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aac648fc-10fc-5899-80de-3f61d32db10b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316080} :answer-field/id #uuid "64b6d89f-f278-5217-96ed-2b3d7bf492cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316785}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3767254e-f5e7-559c-aca3-b6417b0458c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-34211" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨-1,3,5⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨1,-5,-7⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨1,-8,-10⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t &=1 \\\\ 3s-5t &=-8 \\\\ 5s-7t &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & -7 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -7 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t &=1 \\\\ -2t &=-5 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2t=-5\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+t & =1 \\\\ -s+\\frac{5}{2} & =1 \\\\ -s & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ s & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=\\frac{3}{2},\\,t=\\frac{5}{2},$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle s\\cdot t=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{15}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "285f60c4-cfc6-509d-a8ca-df316a92348e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238408} {:answer/id #uuid "306f3ae9-9703-5c61-9e1f-a029efeb6fbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238477} {:answer/id #uuid "7197f81b-8003-5f00-b98f-69a60e60b685" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239030} {:answer/id #uuid "7aef6609-8c36-5411-ba86-81d4a40f69b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239115} {:answer/id #uuid "db09174f-1cdc-5bdb-8120-63756b097fdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db09174f-1cdc-5bdb-8120-63756b097fdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239966} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5dbe15-3666-592c-9f7a-5c21bff9ad15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240504}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "edff4129-bf9d-5206-854e-d3e5b43ca237" :question/math-academy-id "q-105253" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c},$ $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨-1,3,2⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨5,-5,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t &=5 \\\\ 3s-t &=-5 \\\\ 2s-t &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t &=5 \\\\ t &=2 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =5 \\\\ -s+2(2) & =5 \\\\ -s+4 & =5 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=-\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot 2=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "202fca4b-d4db-559c-86f9-155db3d13c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238333} {:answer/id #uuid "2b56c1db-87eb-5ec9-914d-30a522b26fe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238442} {:answer/id #uuid "6182bb36-df22-5b55-8de2-18be6f4e6edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238911} {:answer/id #uuid "a846d2c7-f2b2-52b6-aa5d-db3effda179c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239517} {:answer/id #uuid "f503a4ab-d69a-5e93-a2e0-b67020545fa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6182bb36-df22-5b55-8de2-18be6f4e6edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238911} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f36fa9-d65b-5d54-8f7f-9bbf30419197" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240360}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "caedc8c2-ba3c-5e61-ad1f-0d5eafbb8652" :question/math-academy-id "q-105257" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c},$ $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨1,-2,-1⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨-4,5,-1⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨1,1,4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-4t &=1 \\\\ -2s+5t &=1 \\\\ -s-t &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-4t &=1 \\\\ t &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-4t & =1 \\\\ s-4(-1) & =1 \\\\ s+4 & =1 \\\\ s & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-3,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=-3\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-3)\\cdot (-1)=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241024 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d43760f-5307-568e-a84e-682220ff1a4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238868} {:answer/id #uuid "880f352c-1248-5802-aad6-0f18fb03e119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239238} {:answer/id #uuid "9f0f8258-6bb9-5599-9ae6-72aed7ee6ef6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239444} {:answer/id #uuid "bc37d1db-6d5f-55cb-9d65-e53eb7a7a21a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239696} {:answer/id #uuid "becf26eb-4fe8-5d5a-9c5d-01dc6db2f13e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc37d1db-6d5f-55cb-9d65-e53eb7a7a21a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239696} :answer-field/id #uuid "8da127e5-a769-5b87-898c-b652f5625bd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240581}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1b477b81-717a-5a90-91d6-e069d7ac13b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-105261" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c},$ $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨1,-1,3⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨-2,4,-3⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨3,-7,3⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-2t &=3 \\\\ -s+4t &=-7 \\\\ 3s-3t &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-2t &=3 \\\\ t &=-2 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-2t & =3 \\\\ s-2(-2) & =3 \\\\ s+4 & =3 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=-2,$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=-\\mathbf{b}-2\\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot (-2)=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "145063fc-8e8e-5c5e-b9c0-4ce50643aeca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238221} {:answer/id #uuid "4fd14ba1-3c05-5721-9490-57e8bf80fea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238742} {:answer/id #uuid "a01540c4-5818-561d-9151-d28aeb0e7fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239452} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e4047e-41ea-50d0-ab94-58e7363cb874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239637} {:answer/id #uuid "ebdd9058-9132-5515-90b7-33b231320d45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fd14ba1-3c05-5721-9490-57e8bf80fea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238742} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dee8bc9-1a1f-59f0-8b66-162d23f34c3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240468}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8c4cb4f7-2d57-5ca9-8ffa-a4fe4548b0de" :question/math-academy-id "q-105265" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c},$ $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨-1,-1,4⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨-3,-8,14⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨5,-10,-14⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t &=5 \\\\ -s-8t &=-10 \\\\ 4s+14t &=-14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t &=5 \\\\ t &=3 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s-3t & =5 \\\\ -s-3(3) & =5 \\\\ -s-9 & =5 \\\\ s & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-14,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=-14\\mathbf{b}+3\\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-14)\\cdot 3=-42.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ca81bd-a843-517f-a7ef-72a2701907bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315161} {:answer/id #uuid "31e52722-b368-5c85-8ea5-9c73d21f221f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315408} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3a18e5-9318-5ff6-9f5d-5297ea2e47b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315452} {:answer/id #uuid "43670fca-c17e-5839-b7bf-2ab9ba603b7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315509} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0a632c-b0f2-53fa-9828-61b94974deed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43670fca-c17e-5839-b7bf-2ab9ba603b7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315509} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed15606e-311e-585d-8930-70b904dd77b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317109}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "725d2e8b-44d5-5b25-872e-7c29b876b698" :question/math-academy-id "q-34212" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c},$ $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨1,7,-3⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨-8,10,-4⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨6,9,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-8t &=6 \\\\ 7s+10t &=9 \\\\ -3s-4t &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 10 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{66}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+28{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-8t &=6 \\\\ t &=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-8t & =6 \\\\ s-8\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) & =6 \\\\ s+4 & =6 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=2\\mathbf{b}-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18285e78-b775-52d3-9ce4-8875b58cd9dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339343} {:answer/id #uuid "1be7024d-e144-5979-8991-a6fe697cbc56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339367} {:answer/id #uuid "39886f7e-3d38-5ba7-ae30-319ca5a0cc0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339646} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3953fd-8be9-5eec-b885-1d99ddc7adf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340246} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9dd147-f938-5d4d-8bda-da9705de4409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1be7024d-e144-5979-8991-a6fe697cbc56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339367} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ed9efb-9d03-53c8-9fad-57fa155b57a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341732}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55c44296-8bfb-53c1-b37c-07eab30d99a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-74598" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨-1,2,3⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨3,-7,-9⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨2,-3,-6⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t &=2 \\\\ 2s-7t &=-3 \\\\ 3s-9t &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t &=2 \\\\ -t &=1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-t=1\\,⟹\\,t=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+3t & =2 \\\\ -s+3(-1) & =2 \\\\ -s & =5 \\\\ s & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-5,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=-5\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-5)\\cdot (-1)=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2486b2f1-5c38-55cd-a205-21e202e09c4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339446} {:answer/id #uuid "2cadd916-ed59-5b50-9446-268229ac2732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339516} {:answer/id #uuid "4cc45ccf-adc7-53ad-a852-af95cfc40061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339825} {:answer/id #uuid "733ba44c-1a53-5f59-af78-2d354dda43f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340150} {:answer/id #uuid "7caedebc-c212-5602-b507-20831a0f0c1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cadd916-ed59-5b50-9446-268229ac2732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339516} :answer-field/id #uuid "520ff562-4653-55df-b4dc-8fbcaed97a63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341528}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6c3f74b-5a27-519e-8d22-1736702759dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-74599" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨-1,4,3⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨1,-6,-7⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨1,-10,-15⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t &=1 \\\\ 4s-6t &=-10 \\\\ 3s-7t &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -6 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t &=1 \\\\ -2t &=-6 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2t=-6\\,⟹\\,t=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+t & =1 \\\\ -s+3 & =1 \\\\ -s & =-2 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=2\\mathbf{b}+3\\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot 3=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b3b852-a49c-5eeb-92f6-f26e6d188a47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339184} {:answer/id #uuid "191397de-4f1f-5ce1-a2c1-b8de6e1df5ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339350} {:answer/id #uuid "459245c0-1823-5440-b561-9af08e968b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339745} {:answer/id #uuid "6e7685b0-ef1b-58de-ad96-cbeee1b70636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340105} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd09f6d-fcdf-5876-9523-8e01ec65ed87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e7685b0-ef1b-58de-ad96-cbeee1b70636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340105} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bebdfbe-9cbd-5971-9a6a-74e16cc92f99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341655}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dcb29558-7233-531f-8a7f-7d0b5b7173b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-74602" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨1,7,-6⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨-2,-10,12⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨2,11,-12⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-2t &=2 \\\\ 7s-10t &=11 \\\\ -6s+12t &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -10 & 11 \\\\ -6 & 12 & -12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 12 & -12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-2t &=2 \\\\ 4t &=-3 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n4t=-3\\,⟹\\,t=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-2t & =2 \\\\ s-2\\left(-\\frac{3}{4}\\right) & =2 \\\\ s+\\frac{3}{2} & =2 \\\\ s & =2-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ s & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=\\frac{1}{2},\\,t=-\\frac{3}{4},$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}-\\frac{3}{4}\\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle s\\cdot t=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{3}{4}\\right)=-\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66b81663-6e80-51d7-a913-48b15173205e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343109} {:answer/id #uuid "8714c620-1893-528d-8182-61236ee13206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343405} {:answer/id #uuid "b53eaae6-d50b-5fbe-95be-daf4107639c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343824} {:answer/id #uuid "ec48cbca-b54e-529c-a456-f0f5a7c0d8b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344311} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0d8fa3-1d8c-594e-b99a-40e3f03c6dce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef0d8fa3-1d8c-594e-b99a-40e3f03c6dce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344340} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a27d35b-cc89-5818-8e8d-5ccf5c8819cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344757}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c8c4efc9-6266-5ebb-8bcb-7388b1494f8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74605" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c},$ $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨1,3,6⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨1,-2,4⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨3,19,-10⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 19 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+t &=3 \\\\ 3s-2t &=19 \\\\ 6s+4t &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 19 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -28\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -28\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -32\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-32,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7eb8a46-2267-5072-8709-51251ce9e760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393419} {:answer/id #uuid "4af5620d-a92f-5f04-b9d9-0982f3d2a131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393420} {:answer/id #uuid "9db239d2-39ff-503c-9288-54070e1b2d71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393421} {:answer/id #uuid "145d4992-30fd-5d3a-9dbb-d5d2652afc6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393422} {:answer/id #uuid "fbde74ee-e78a-57a1-9751-28a91866994f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9db239d2-39ff-503c-9288-54070e1b2d71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393421} :answer-field/id #uuid "b06e84e5-8b15-54ef-8727-430594345689" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393418}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4018a53f-b299-52cf-a135-1013bf76ce32" :question/math-academy-id "q-74607" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨3,8,-7⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨9,22,-5⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+3t &=9 \\\\ 2s+8t &=22 \\\\ 3s-7t &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -16 & -32\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+3t &=9 \\\\ 2t &=4 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2t=4\\,⟹\\,t=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s+3t & =9 \\\\ s+3(2) & =9 \\\\ s & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=3,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=3\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=3\\cdot 2=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5469c2f4-10d4-551a-8387-1f41e195f9f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399463} {:answer/id #uuid "b5aaf75e-0319-5e2f-b6a1-406f9f457622" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399464} {:answer/id #uuid "6f0f386a-54e4-5bbd-999d-c5b1e894fea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399465} {:answer/id #uuid "ea345608-0f4c-5f8a-9cea-a53c46ba68a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399466} {:answer/id #uuid "f370dd07-5630-5589-a9df-b8eef801b693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f370dd07-5630-5589-a9df-b8eef801b693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399467} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ded2025-f849-5e24-ae50-154d00e66f84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399462}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da64bb93-914e-5229-bb6d-b7d97e6fa1bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105248" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨1,-4,2⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨3,-10,2⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨-2,5,0⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+3t &=-2 \\\\ -4s-10t &=5 \\\\ 2s+2t &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -10 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-2,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403766 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e98f85e7-255d-57c4-987f-635dd16edd05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403768} {:answer/id #uuid "22eae911-bfae-55d1-acf2-f7cf5e10e29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403769} {:answer/id #uuid "a100b320-8f04-5bdd-8ea7-26f1cec017c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403770} {:answer/id #uuid "b4645d11-c80f-53cc-afba-0d87d9de8fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403771} {:answer/id #uuid "d43a8623-8d3d-5185-9200-86c7e4e420c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d43a8623-8d3d-5185-9200-86c7e4e420c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403772} :answer-field/id #uuid "b97ac01d-f426-551c-8b2f-1c4b7bdf001e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403767}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da2b75e4-b38a-5b5b-9891-19906308bd00" :question/math-academy-id "q-74600" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\mathrm{Π}:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, $t,s\\in \\mathbb{R}$, where  $\\mathbf{b}=⟨-1,4,-5⟩$, $\\mathbf{c}=⟨3,-9,15⟩$, and  $\\mathbf{u}=⟨2,-2,11⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in \\mathrm{Π}$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c} & =\\mathbf{u} \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t &=2 \\\\ 4s-9t &=-2 \\\\ -5s+15t &=11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -9 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=1,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31aa51c7-7bbf-539a-8251-ca7e5420f8e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421502} {:answer/id #uuid "404186fe-c6bf-5419-b373-a5941944a534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421505} {:answer/id #uuid "a5aeef05-ac8e-5ffc-b5cd-7dab5e605fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421514} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1bdf10-0234-549d-b4c6-dcf3de7b6fdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421517} {:answer/id #uuid "ffbc367b-e607-5dad-b444-946e25112421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31aa51c7-7bbf-539a-8251-ca7e5420f8e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421502} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe4e956c-1b1f-5312-af0b-3bb85188fdbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421527}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b9c3557-0777-5517-a4eb-de326b8ca141" :question/math-academy-id "q-74609" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,3⟩$, $c=⟨2,-6,-4⟩$, and  $u=⟨3,-7,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t &=3 \\\\ 4s-6t &=-7 \\\\ 3s-4t &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t &=3 \\\\ 2t &=5 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2t=5\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =3 \\\\ -s+2\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right) & =3 \\\\ -s+5 & =3 \\\\ -s & =-2 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=\\frac{5}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b+\\frac{5}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The repeated equation does not cause inconsistency. The third coordinate gives the missing independent equation." :answer/id #uuid "50be0dbb-729f-527e-a8dd-e4bcd0b394c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713322} {:answer/feedback "This is $t$. The requested value is $s\\cdot t$." :answer/id #uuid "91a39ad4-cd8c-5671-9d2f-0a41cbe97000" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713329} {:answer/feedback "Yes. The pair $(4,-1)$ satisfies all three coordinates and has product $-4$." :answer/id #uuid "a80f81d5-d260-5a89-ba0f-55d6260788ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713331} {:answer/feedback "This is the sum $s+t$. Use the product after checking membership." :answer/id #uuid "ed295388-d435-5252-b201-efc65f104216" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713335} {:answer/feedback "This is $s$. Multiply it by $t=-1$." :answer/id #uuid "f884e554-fb60-56f5-9de4-d70b8aac748d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Yes. The pair $(4,-1)$ satisfies all three coordinates and has product $-4$." :answer/id #uuid "a80f81d5-d260-5a89-ba0f-55d6260788ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713331} :answer-field/id #uuid "201e8260-65cd-578b-8403-3aa3a5fdf53e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713320}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "016710be-ea4e-545b-b717-b22ccfc9d1eb" :question/problem "Determine whether $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, where $s,t\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1, 2, 1\\rangle,\\qquad\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 2, 4, -1\\rangle,\\qquad\\mathbf{u}=\\langle 2, 4, 5\\rangle.\n$$\n\nIf it does, select the value of $s\\cdot t$ in $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$. Otherwise, select the statement that $\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$." :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in\\Pi$ exactly when the same values of $s$ and $t$ satisfy all three coordinate equations. Expanding gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+2t &=2 \\\\ 2s+4t &=4 \\\\ s-t &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe second equation repeats twice the first, so those two equations alone cannot determine both coefficients. Use the third coordinate as well. Apply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-2R_1$ and $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nInterchange $R_2$ and $R_3$ to put the nonzero row above the zero row:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThen $-3t=3$ gives $t=-1$, and $s+2(-1)=2$ gives $s=4$. Check every coordinate:\n\n$$\n4\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 4-2,8-4,4+1\\rangle=\\langle 2,4,5\\rangle=\\mathbf{u}.\n$$\n\nThere is no contradiction; the zero row adds no restriction. The remaining two equations determine a unique pair. Therefore $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on $\\Pi$ and $s\\cdot t=4(-1)=-4$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This product uses a pair that fails the third coordinate. Membership must be checked first." :answer/id #uuid "6dd423a0-ae3b-5e13-87cc-e1d1e5e969ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713326} {:answer/feedback "The first coordinate is not the requested product, and the system is inconsistent." :answer/id #uuid "840a29b9-d0a1-585b-96ee-1232f063e2ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713327} {:answer/feedback "A product from a partial system does not establish membership; check all three coordinates." :answer/id #uuid "87c06dd6-1497-50e0-b49f-866d36ca3ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713328} {:answer/feedback "This is the candidate value of $t$, and that candidate fails the third coordinate." :answer/id #uuid "aed8b987-c1df-5e0c-932e-77f4160d8f36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713332} {:answer/feedback "Yes. Row reduction gives $0=1$, so no pair works." :answer/id #uuid "b916a909-f5f4-5a9c-a5eb-5a772a786063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Yes. Row reduction gives $0=1$, so no pair works." :answer/id #uuid "b916a909-f5f4-5a9c-a5eb-5a772a786063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713333} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f478c4-d46b-515a-9e5a-0d9001327484" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713337}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4bd375d4-5b1f-5bdb-83be-769624674385" :question/problem "Determine whether $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, where $s,t\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1, 1, 2\\rangle,\\qquad\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 1, -1, 1\\rangle,\\qquad\\mathbf{u}=\\langle 1, 3, 4\\rangle.\n$$\n\nIf it does, select the value of $s\\cdot t$ in $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$. Otherwise, select the statement that $\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$." :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in\\Pi$ exactly when the same values of $s$ and $t$ satisfy all three coordinate equations. Expanding the vector equation gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+t &=1 \\\\ s-t &=3 \\\\ 2s+t &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSet up the augmented matrix and apply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-R_1$ and $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-2R_1$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNow apply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-\\frac12 R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row says $0=1$, a contradiction. The first two coordinate equations would give $t=-1$ and $s=2$, but then the third coordinate would be $2s+t=3$, not $4$. Thus no pair satisfies all three equations. The vector $\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$; the candidate product $-2$ from only the first two equations is not a valid answer."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The signs of $s=2$ and $t=-1$ differ, so their product is negative." :answer/id #uuid "05eed988-5442-593c-88d6-9715f575714b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713318} {:answer/feedback "Yes. The pair $(2,-1)$ satisfies every coordinate, and its product is $-2$." :answer/id #uuid "10f26121-320a-57ba-bb34-5ddef5eaf638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713319} {:answer/feedback "The third equation holds: $2+2(-1)=0$." :answer/id #uuid "686fc79b-533a-5d0a-a7f5-10ce4acd911b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713324} {:answer/feedback "This is $s+t$. The requested quantity is $s\\cdot t$." :answer/id #uuid "6ce0be00-e792-5eea-945f-513eaacf83f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713325} {:answer/feedback "This is $t$ alone. Multiply $s$ and $t$." :answer/id #uuid "98bdb059-ba2d-5996-8775-8e7e5e78d2a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Yes. The pair $(2,-1)$ satisfies every coordinate, and its product is $-2$." :answer/id #uuid "10f26121-320a-57ba-bb34-5ddef5eaf638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713319} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f92007e-156e-5ad4-b687-e9324b1fd2da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713323}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e81cdfbb-d407-58ff-998e-36733206e347" :question/problem "Determine whether $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, where $s,t\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1, 0, 1\\rangle,\\qquad\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 0, 1, 2\\rangle,\\qquad\\mathbf{u}=\\langle 2, -1, 0\\rangle.\n$$\n\nIf it does, select the value of $s\\cdot t$ in $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$. Otherwise, select the statement that $\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$.\n\nUse the component equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s &=2 \\\\ t &=-1 \\\\ s+2t &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nCheck that the values from the first two equations also satisfy the third." :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in\\Pi$ exactly when the same values of $s$ and $t$ satisfy all three coordinate equations. The component system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s &=2 \\\\ t &=-1 \\\\ s+2t &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe first two equations give $s=2$ and $t=-1$. In the third equation, $s+2t=2+2(-1)=0$, as required. Equivalently,\n\n$$\n2\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 2,-1,0\\rangle=\\mathbf{u}.\n$$\n\nAll three coordinates agree, so $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on $\\Pi$ and $s\\cdot t=2(-1)=-2$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713652 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Check all three coordinates before giving a product; the system has no common solution." :answer/id #uuid "2ab2cccf-0bb2-54be-9ce0-3c0abc5be8e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713649} {:answer/feedback "Correct. The coordinate system is inconsistent." :answer/id #uuid "6710d9a6-e649-5e6f-8a86-0550e270dcb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713657} {:answer/feedback "Check all three coordinates before giving a product; the system has no common solution." :answer/id #uuid "78683cc2-0462-5abd-92cb-c091eaa949ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713666} {:answer/feedback "Check all three coordinates before giving a product; the system has no common solution." :answer/id #uuid "a42f9ea5-e752-57a1-9570-2deaa0a51218" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713673} {:answer/feedback "Check all three coordinates before giving a product; the system has no common solution." :answer/id #uuid "b18c3309-58d6-5a38-b6d0-f78f92585710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct. The coordinate system is inconsistent." :answer/id #uuid "6710d9a6-e649-5e6f-8a86-0550e270dcb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713657} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cde8873-1bf6-5e5e-8e61-11ad2fe1dfb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713668}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "397ab5f1-714c-50a0-886a-dd99b0d87a5b" :question/problem "Determine whether $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, where $s,t\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{b}&=\\langle -2, 2, -2\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{c}&=\\langle -3, -1, 3\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{u}&=\\langle 15, 2, -10\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf it does, select the value of $s\\cdot t$ in $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$. Otherwise, select the statement that $\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$." :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in\\Pi$ exactly when the same values of $s$ and $t$ satisfy all three coordinate equations. Expanding the vector equation gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2s-3t &=15 \\\\ 2s-t &=2 \\\\ -2s+3t &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSet up the augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -10\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2 \\leftarrow R_2-(-1)R_1$, then $R_3 \\leftarrow R_3-(1)R_1$, then $R_3 \\leftarrow R_3-\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row gives $0=\\frac{1}{2}$, a contradiction. No pair satisfies all three equations. Thus $\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$. A product obtained from only two coordinates is not a valid answer."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713667 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This uses $s+t$ instead of $s\\cdot t$." :answer/id #uuid "5d358bb8-9917-51d4-aaeb-7c96047880fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713656} {:answer/feedback "The pair $s=0,t=-2$ satisfies all three coordinates; the vector lies on the plane." :answer/id #uuid "6846e198-8e22-5428-8ca2-2e91f853a917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713658} {:answer/feedback "This uses $s^2+t^2$ instead of $s\\cdot t$." :answer/id #uuid "6fc68ecf-97f3-5c95-bc6d-4965b97abcbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713661} {:answer/feedback "Correct. The common pair satisfies all three equations and gives $s\\cdot t=0$." :answer/id #uuid "7691cdd3-7761-5524-ba89-8b3617873584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713665} {:answer/feedback "This uses $s-t$ instead of $s\\cdot t$." :answer/id #uuid "b2a59cc9-3021-5c24-8c5c-4fc559c55718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct. The common pair satisfies all three equations and gives $s\\cdot t=0$." :answer/id #uuid "7691cdd3-7761-5524-ba89-8b3617873584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713665} :answer-field/id #uuid "5121c8ed-3e06-5e06-8005-63a610a406a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713654}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8496c6a9-e8f5-5ea8-a3eb-410a86fc5225" :question/problem "Determine whether $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, where $s,t\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{b}&=\\langle -2, -1, -2\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{c}&=\\langle -1, -3, 1\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{u}&=\\langle 2, 6, -2\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf it does, select the value of $s\\cdot t$ in $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$. Otherwise, select the statement that $\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$." :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in\\Pi$ exactly when the same values of $s$ and $t$ satisfy all three coordinate equations. Expanding the vector equation gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2s-t &=2 \\\\ -s-3t &=6 \\\\ -2s+t &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSet up the augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2 \\leftarrow R_2-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_1$, then $R_3 \\leftarrow R_3-(1)R_1$, then $R_3 \\leftarrow R_3-\\left(-\\frac{4}{5}\\right)R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{5}{2} & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row is $0=0$, so it adds no restriction. Back substitute in the two nonzero rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t&=\\frac{5}{-\\frac{5}{2}}=-2 \\\\ s&=\\frac{2-(-1)(-2)}{-2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nVerify every coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)(-2)+(-2)(-1)&=2=2 \\\\ (0)(-1)+(-2)(-3)&=6=6 \\\\ (0)(-2)+(-2)(1)&=-2=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll three coordinates agree, so the vector lies on the plane. Therefore,\n\n$$\ns\\cdot t=(0)\\cdot(-2)=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Correct. The coordinate system is inconsistent." :answer/id #uuid "28738f3c-3a3b-5f3d-a6aa-50cb4e0f13ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713648} {:answer/feedback "Check all three coordinates before giving a product; the system has no common solution." :answer/id #uuid "35ab9ab8-b60c-5dd8-b84a-10f94d5b3491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713651} {:answer/feedback "Check all three coordinates before giving a product; the system has no common solution." :answer/id #uuid "5a1fd843-a892-5d68-a1bc-03b05a719513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713655} {:answer/feedback "Check all three coordinates before giving a product; the system has no common solution." :answer/id #uuid "7339d2a2-5161-5528-81ed-ce73e38fab83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713663} {:answer/feedback "Check all three coordinates before giving a product; the system has no common solution." :answer/id #uuid "f98189a4-d135-5e50-bf2c-dfccb96c4bdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct. The coordinate system is inconsistent." :answer/id #uuid "28738f3c-3a3b-5f3d-a6aa-50cb4e0f13ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713648} :answer-field/id #uuid "2daaf91f-9d4c-5640-bd18-fea3ac6f7e25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713650}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec1392b1-fa17-5e2e-b673-e3d4d9a2a12d" :question/problem "Determine whether $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, where $s,t\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{b}&=\\langle 3, -2, 1\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{c}&=\\langle 2, -1, 3\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{u}&=\\langle 2, -1, -4\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf it does, select the value of $s\\cdot t$ in $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$. Otherwise, select the statement that $\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$." :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in\\Pi$ exactly when the same values of $s$ and $t$ satisfy all three coordinate equations. Expanding the vector equation gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+2t &=2 \\\\ -2s-t &=-1 \\\\ s+3t &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSet up the augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2 \\leftarrow R_2-\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)R_1$, then $R_3 \\leftarrow R_3-\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)R_1$, then $R_3 \\leftarrow R_3-(7)R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row gives $0=-7$, a contradiction. No pair satisfies all three equations. Thus $\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$. A product obtained from only two coordinates is not a valid answer."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Correct. The common pair satisfies all three equations and gives $s\\cdot t=-3$." :answer/id #uuid "42b99840-4e1a-5ce7-a8ac-f183adf96f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713653} {:answer/feedback "This uses $s+t$ instead of $s\\cdot t$." :answer/id #uuid "6acfcd37-40eb-5a7a-b7db-dfad25fa5463" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713659} {:answer/feedback "This uses $s^2+t^2$ instead of $s\\cdot t$." :answer/id #uuid "95ff6a7d-ce7c-578d-8318-d8b08d81b7e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713671} {:answer/feedback "This uses $s-t$ instead of $s\\cdot t$." :answer/id #uuid "a19283dc-f0fd-57da-b5c8-d3a92928e994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713672} {:answer/feedback "The pair $s=-3,t=1$ satisfies all three coordinates; the vector lies on the plane." :answer/id #uuid "b1acdd3b-99ff-5f71-b924-c847bf554e0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct. The common pair satisfies all three equations and gives $s\\cdot t=-3$." :answer/id #uuid "42b99840-4e1a-5ce7-a8ac-f183adf96f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713653} :answer-field/id #uuid "9096c7ae-667d-5cd0-9aa3-b112b40b5d45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713669}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef68a12e-b7bd-5bfe-bfd3-f42a50d17393" :question/problem "Determine whether $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$, where $s,t\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{b}&=\\langle -1, 1, 3\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{c}&=\\langle -3, -3, -2\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf{u}&=\\langle 0, -6, -11\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf it does, select the value of $s\\cdot t$ in $\\mathbf{u}=s\\mathbf{b}+t\\mathbf{c}$. Otherwise, select the statement that $\\mathbf{u}$ does not lie on $\\Pi$." :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u}\\in\\Pi$ exactly when the same values of $s$ and $t$ satisfy all three coordinate equations. Expanding the vector equation gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t &=0 \\\\ s-3t &=-6 \\\\ 3s-2t &=-11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSet up the augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -11\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2 \\leftarrow R_2-(-1)R_1$, then $R_3 \\leftarrow R_3-(-3)R_1$, then $R_3 \\leftarrow R_3-\\left(\\frac{11}{6}\\right)R_2$:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row is $0=0$, so it adds no restriction. Back substitute in the two nonzero rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t&=\\frac{-6}{-6}=1 \\\\ s&=\\frac{0-(-3)(1)}{-1}=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nVerify every coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)(-1)+(1)(-3)&=0=0 \\\\ (-3)(1)+(1)(-3)&=-6=-6 \\\\ (-3)(3)+(1)(-2)&=-11=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll three coordinates agree, so the vector lies on the plane. Therefore,\n\n$$\ns\\cdot t=(-3)\\cdot(1)=-3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713681 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This uses $s^2+t^2$ instead of $s\\cdot t$." :answer/id #uuid "0c321f8a-24ec-5db4-b988-8ab237bcc86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713647} {:answer/feedback "This uses $s-t$ instead of $s\\cdot t$." :answer/id #uuid "6e0cbe62-8517-52b9-b86e-350f8f95bd93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713660} {:answer/feedback "Correct. The common pair satisfies all three equations and gives $s\\cdot t=6$." :answer/id #uuid "701cefd1-6555-5482-b3b3-689d8332b0c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713662} {:answer/feedback "The pair $s=3,t=2$ satisfies all three coordinates; the vector lies on the plane." :answer/id #uuid "75a81b2b-7111-51b5-979e-0e2d6c53b2c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value 